MODULE GDecode
! -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- --   
!The purpose of this MODULE is to read G-code and 3D print models with a ABB robot
!During developement, PrusaSlicer with MARLIN-flavour was used. 
!The module uses special "Extrude" functions as wrapper for CAP move instructions. Trigg movement could also be used. 
!This "Extrude" function must be developed for the specific "extruder" setup.
!Functions used are: ExtrudeLStart ExtrudeL ExtrudeC  ExtrudeLStopp
!
!G10/G11 firmware E-retraction is used to detect where to build
!Only relative E movement supported (M83)
!G0 is not supported, use G1 instead.
!
!G1 movements shorter than "minMovement" are ignored, and skipped completely.
!G2 and G3 movements to short are converted to G1
!Bulding large rotation symmetrical objects? Consider to activate rotateTable for stable build position.  
!This uses an external axis to rotate while the robot is only moving minimaly.
